[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about a wrong date into one ticket. Read by
tenant, channel and report text, the reports have two causes, and a small group inside the first
reads differently. Only `parser` is what the ticket describes.

<Callout>
Merged as one issue, but it is more than one. Each cause needs its own ticket and its own fix.
</Callout>

## The causes

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get a
  flipped month and day. This is the cause #4471 names.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Day-first tenants
  (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) type what the hint says and the form reads it their
  way. Different bug, different fix.
- **One-day shift**: 5 of the `parser` reports (the footnote under the table) are off by one day,
  with day and month intact. A timezone or DST problem is the suspect. Not confirmed. The desk's
  view files them under `parser` by tenant, so they are already inside its count.

## How the reports were counted

- The export repeats some reports. One id is one report (`uniqueById`).
- Intake's tag is a guess from the browser. It is wrong for many reports, so the count uses
  the tenant, the channel and the desk's reading of the report instead.
- Five reports read as a one-day move (`oneDayMove` in `desk-notes.json`): R-41202, R-41209,
  R-41236, R-41344, R-41620. The table counts them under `parser`, where they are filed.
- Three `parser` reports carry no date to check (R-41290, R-41417, R-41514). They are placed by
  tenant only.

## Tickets

One ticket per cause, filed in the public repo
[mattszmigiel/ticket-4471](https://github.com/mattszmigiel/ticket-4471/issues).

